# gadak MCP demo — one line of setup, then a real Claude Code session that
# answers a question no JQL query can express, using the local mirror.
#
# Regenerated by `make media-mcp`, which requires BOTH:
#   bash tools/tapes/prepare.sh          (mirror + binary)
#   bash tools/tapes/prepare-agent.sh    (isolated HOME with Claude Code auth)
# Run `bash tools/tapes/prepare-agent.sh --clean` afterwards — it holds a copy
# of this machine's Claude credentials.
#
# Nothing here is scripted output: the second scene really calls the model,
# which really calls gadak's MCP tools. Takes vary, so re-run until one reads
# well. Everything visible comes from the demo mirror (examples/demo.db).
#
# Sizing mirrors the other terminal tapes: 77 cols × 24 rows, font 20, README
# renders this at 800 px. See the sizing note in agent.tape before changing it.
#
# Theme: try gadak-paper first (same identity as search.gif / agent.gif). If
# Claude Code's own ANSI is unreadable on paper, fall back to a dark theme
# and record why in the take notes (docs/project/MEDIA.md).
#
# Size: the committed asset is this tape's output run through
# `gifsicle -O3 --colors 64` (see docs/project/MEDIA.md). If still over 3.5 MB, cut
# the idle tail (frame range is picked per take).

Output docs/media/mcp.gif
Output docs/media/mcp.mp4

Set Shell "bash"
Set FontSize 20
Set FontFamily "D2Coding, Menlo, Monaco, monospace"
Set Width 1080
Set Height 620
Set Theme {"name":"gadak-paper","background":"#f4efe4","foreground":"#1c1812","cursor":"#2e4560","selection_background":"#d5dde8","black":"#1c1812","red":"#8f3530","green":"#2f5e42","yellow":"#8a6418","blue":"#2f5d8c","magenta":"#2e4560","cyan":"#2a4159","white":"#e4d9c4","brightBlack":"#635a4f","brightRed":"#8f3530","brightGreen":"#2f5e42","brightYellow":"#8a6418","brightBlue":"#2e4560","brightMagenta":"#2e4560","brightCyan":"#2a4159","brightWhite":"#f4efe4"}
Set Padding 14
Set Framerate 8
Set TypingSpeed 45ms
Set WindowBar Colorful
Set BorderRadius 6
Set WaitTimeout 120s

# Neutral shell: no user@host, no real $HOME path. HOME points at the throwaway
# agent home, so the paths Claude Code prints below carry no identity.
Hide
Set TypingSpeed 1ms
# `|| exit 1` is a safety interlock, not tidiness: without env-agent.sh the
# shell would keep going with the *operator's* real HOME and no GADAK_HOME, and
# the take would record a live Jira mirror. Fail the recording instead.
Type "source tools/tapes/.tmp/env-agent.sh || exit 1"
Enter
# pin-demo.sh (written by make media-mcp into the isolated HOME): copies the
# demo mirror to $HOME/.gadak, puts gadak on $HOME/bin, and sets
# disableClaudeAiConnectors so claude.ai connectors do not enter the frame.
Type "source /private/tmp/gadak-demo/pin-demo.sh"
Enter
Type "clear"
Enter
Set TypingSpeed 45ms
Show

Sleep 500ms

# ── Setup: one line teaches any MCP client about the mirror ────────────────
Type "claude mcp add gadak -- gadak mcp"
Enter
Sleep 2.5s

Type "clear"
Enter
Sleep 400ms

# mcp add refreshes oauthAccount (email, displayName) into ~/.claude.json.
# Strip those before the TUI opens, and pin the demo GADAK_HOME so the
# spawned `gadak mcp` cannot fall through to the operator's real mirror.
Hide
Set TypingSpeed 1ms
Type "python3 /private/tmp/gadak-demo/strip-oauth.py"
Enter
Type "clear"
Enter
Set TypingSpeed 45ms
Show

# ── The session: one question, both sources ────────────────────────────────
# Deliberately not a reopen_count question — that field carries the README
# quick start and the agent clip already. This asks the thing Jira cannot
# answer at all, because the wiki is a second search: 'idempotency' is in 7
# issues and 4 pages of examples/demo.db, and one FTS index holds both.
Type "claude"
Enter
Sleep 5s

Type "Search our Jira and wiki for idempotency. Answer in 3 lines."
Sleep 600ms
Enter

# The model works here: tool calls to gadak_search stream in as they happen.
# The wait a viewer sees is the model's, not gadak's — the mirror answers in
# milliseconds, and a slow take reads as if the local file were the slow part.
# So extended thinking is off (prepare-agent.sh). Haiku was tried and rejected:
# it called gadak_search with the wrong argument name twice and then reported
# "zero results" instead of the error — fast, and confidently wrong on camera.
# Hold on the answered frame — do not Ctrl+C (that prints a resume UUID).
Sleep 11s
